  "summary_en": "European Commission 2012 proposal for a Regulation replacing Directive 98/79/EC on in vitro diagnostic medical devices. It introduces four risk classes, stricter notified body oversight, UDI traceability, the Eudamed database, clinical performance study rules and vigilance reporting. It is not about AI or robotics.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Four-class risk-based classification (A–D) with proportionate conformity assessment",
   "Stricter designation and monitoring of notified bodies, including unannounced inspections",
   "Unique Device Identification and Eudamed central database with public transparency",
   "Clinical performance study rules and serious incident reporting within 15 days",
   "Medical Device Coordination Group created; repeals Directive 98/79/EC, applies five years after entry into force"
  ],
